in our previous lessons We performed a  simplified version of the rna-seq using  the T by info platform but did you know  that it is also possible to perform  differential gene expression analysis at  the end of the standard rnec pipeline  you will explore this briefly in this  video note that in this demo pipeline we  are making use of samples that were  taken from humanized mice with implanted  tumors and our aim here is to First  generate gene expression tables from the  raw RNA secrets and perform differential  gene expression analysis now let us  click on the start to build a pipeline  the steps remain the same as we have  covered in a previous video first we  have the pre-processing step that makes  use of trinomatic  and PCR clean  and note that the functions of each of  the algorithms have been explained in  the pop-ups that show when you click on  that particular step so feel free to  browse through and learn at your own  pace  so for now let's click on bow tie2t  algorithm for mapping on the transcripts  and are some expression table for  quantifying Gene and isoform abundances  and finally let's click on the desect2  option for differential gene expression  analysis  and then click on end  and with that the pipeline is ready we  have performed the differential gene  expression analysis within a standard  rnac pipeline in our next video we will  discuss what are the various outputs and  how to interpret them
 

